\title{Thoughts on pedagogy and community-building}
\author{brentyorgey}

\p{This semester I am participating in a "teaching square" with several colleagues, where we visit and observe each other's classes—not for the purpose of evaluation, or even constructive criticism, but merely to observe and reflect on our own teaching. On Monday I visited a class taught by one of my colleagues (who shall remain anonymous for now since I don't know whether she would want to be identified publicly in this context).  The class was in a very different discipline than my own, XXX}

\p{This week I also read [[shriramkrishnamurthi]]'s [pedagogy recommendations](https://parentheticallyspeaking.org/articles/pedagogy-recommendations/), XXX}
